{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 40, "model_name": "mistralai/mistral-small-4-119b-2603", "content": "**A Whirlwind Tour of Japan**\n\nJapan is a land where ancient traditions meet cutting-edge modernity, and my recent trip was a whirlwind of unforgettable experiences.\n\nI began in Tokyo, where neon-lit streets and towering skyscrapers create a futuristic vibe. A visit to Senso-ji Temple in Asakusa offered a stark contrast—a serene oasis in the bustling city. Sampling fresh sushi at Tsukiji Outer Market and exploring the quirky shops of Harajuku were highlights.\n\nNext, I took the bullet train to Kyoto, the cultural heart of Japan. Walking through the bamboo grove at Arashiyama and visiting the golden Kinkaku-ji Temple transported me to another era. The serene gardens of Ryoan-ji and the historic Fushimi Inari Shrine, with its endless torii gates, left me in awe.\n\nIn Osaka, the food scene stole the show. Takoyaki, okonomiyaki, and a steaming bowl of ramen at Dotonbori were pure bliss. The lively atmosphere of Universal Studios Japan added a playful touch to the trip.\n\nA side trip to Hiroshima introduced me to the poignant history of Peace Memorial Park, while Miyajima Island’s iconic floating torii gate in the sea was a surreal sight.\n\nFrom the impeccable cleanliness of trains to the kindness of locals, Japan’s hospitality shone through. The blend of old and new, the meticulous attention to detail, and the respect for tradition made this journey extraordinary.\n\nIn just two weeks, Japan left an indelible mark on my heart. I can’t wait to return.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.10948650538921356}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.05375334993004799}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.6028658151626587}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -1.5139465176616795e-05}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Tour", "logprob": -2.472693920135498}, {"token": " of", "logprob": -0.002733900910243392}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -7.25958